IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa1-part2-formation.l4: Part 2 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Company formation, ss 7 to 16
-- (lines 56-221 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every rule cites its provision with @ref and quotes
-- the text on `-- src:` lines (generated from the raw file by srcrefs.py quote, never retyped).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md, Reading a result).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the provision.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words. Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide. Each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent,
--               list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Two kinds of function (NOTES.md, fork F-C1 and F-C2):
--   "the X ... as required" / "states what it must": a requirement is MET. JUST TRUE where at least one requirement applies and
--   every one that applies is met; JUST FALSE where one that applies is not met (a bare "must" not done); NOTHING where no
--   requirement applies.
--   "the X must do Y": the DUTY ARISES. JUST TRUE where the text's "where"/"if" holds; JUST FALSE where it does not.
-- SEAMS. An answer another part computes (s 159A disqualification, s 790C registrable person, s 1110A identity verified, s 86(2)
-- appropriate address, s 1146 authenticated) is taken as a MAYBE BOOLEAN input named for its section, so that NOTHING stays NOTHING.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 2: COMPANY FORMATION (lines 56-221)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 7: Method of forming company ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:58 | 7 Method of forming company
-- src:59 | (1) A company is formed under this Act by one or more persons—
-- src:60 | (a) subscribing their names to a memorandum of association (see section 8), and
-- src:61 | (b) complying with the requirements of this Act as to registration (see sections 9 to 13).
@ref s 7(1) Method of forming company (src:58-61)
GIVEN `number of persons who subscribe their names` IS A NUMBER
      `the persons subscribe their names to a memorandum of association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons comply with the requirements of this Act as to registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the company is formed under this Act` MEANS
    IF       `number of persons who subscribe their names` AT LEAST 1
         AND `the persons subscribe their names to a memorandum of association`
         AND `the persons comply with the requirements of this Act as to registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company is formed under this Act by one or more persons"

-- src:62 | (2) A company may not be so formed for an unlawful purpose.
@ref s 7(2) A company may not be formed for an unlawful purpose (src:62-62)
GIVEN `the purpose for which the company is to be formed is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the company may be formed for the purpose` MEANS
    IF `the purpose for which the company is to be formed is unlawful`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not be so formed for an unlawful purpose"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only "an unlawful purpose" and says nothing of a lawful one

-- ---- s 8: Memorandum of association ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:63 | 8 Memorandum of association
-- src:64 | (1) A memorandum of association is a memorandum stating that the subscribers—
-- src:65 | (a) wish to form a company under this Act, and
-- src:66 | (b) agree to become members of the company and, in the case of a company that is to have a share capital, to take at least one share each.
@ref s 8(1) Memorandum of association (src:63-66)
GIVEN `the memorandum states that the subscribers wish to form a company under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum states that the subscribers agree to become members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum states that each subscriber agrees to take at least one share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) the document is a memorandum of association` MEANS
    IF       `the memorandum states that the subscribers wish to form a company under this Act`
         AND `the memorandum states that the subscribers agree to become members of the company`
         AND (   (NOT `the company is to have a share capital`)
              OR `the memorandum states that each subscriber agrees to take at least one share`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A memorandum of association is a memorandum stating that the subscribers— (a) wish to form a company under this Act, and (b) agree to become members of the company and, in the case of a company that is to have a share capital, to take at least one share each"

-- src:67 | (2) The memorandum must be in the prescribed form and must be authenticated by each subscriber.
@ref s 8(2) Memorandum of association: prescribed form and authentication (src:67-67)
GIVEN `the memorandum is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1146 the memorandum is authenticated by each subscriber` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) the memorandum meets the requirements as to form and authentication` MEANS
    IF NOT `the memorandum is in the prescribed form`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The memorandum must be in the prescribed form" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1146 the memorandum is authenticated by each subscriber`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "authenticated" is defined in s 1146
         WHEN JUST authenticated THEN
             IF authenticated
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be authenticated by each subscriber" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

DECLARE `s 8(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(2) authenticate the memorandum`

@ref s 8(2) Memorandum of association: authentication by each subscriber (src:67-67)
`s 8(2) the subscriber's duty` MEANS
    PARTY `Subscriber to the memorandum`
    MUST `s 8(2) authenticate the memorandum`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Subscriber to the memorandum` BECAUSE "the memorandum was not authenticated by the subscriber"

-- ---- s 9: Registration documents -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:69 | 9 Registration documents
-- src:70 | (1) The memorandum of association must be delivered to the registrar together with an application for registration of the company, the documents required by this section and a statement of compliance.
@ref s 9(1) Registration documents: what is delivered to the registrar (src:69-70)
GIVEN `the memorandum of association is delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application for registration of the company is delivered with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents required by section 9 are delivered with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of compliance is delivered with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) the delivery includes what the section requires` MEANS
    IF       `the memorandum of association is delivered to the registrar`
         AND `an application for registration of the company is delivered with it`
         AND `the documents required by section 9 are delivered with it`
         AND `a statement of compliance is delivered with it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The memorandum of association must be delivered to the registrar together with an application for registration of the company, the documents required by this section and a statement of compliance" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:71 | (2) The application for registration must state—
-- src:72 | (a) the company's proposed name,
-- src:73 | (b) whether the company's registered office is to be situated in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland,
-- src:74 | (c) whether the liability of the members of the company is to be limited, and if so whether it is to be limited by shares or by guarantee, ...
-- src:75 | (d) whether the company is to be a private or a public company , and
-- src:76 | (e) that the subscribers wish to form the company for lawful purposes.
@ref s 9(2) Registration documents: what the application must state (src:71-76)
GIVEN `the application states the company's proposed name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application states whether the registered office is to be in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application states whether the liability of the members is to be limited, and if so whether by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application states whether the company is to be a private or a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application states that the subscribers wish to form the company for lawful purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the application states what it must` MEANS
    IF       `the application states the company's proposed name`
         AND `the application states whether the registered office is to be in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland`
         AND `the application states whether the liability of the members is to be limited, and if so whether by shares or by guarantee`
         AND `the application states whether the company is to be a private or a public company`
         AND `the application states that the subscribers wish to form the company for lawful purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application for registration must state— (a) ... (e)" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:77 | (3) If the application is delivered by a person as agent for the subscribers to the memorandum of association, it must state his name and address.
@ref s 9(3) Registration documents: application delivered by an agent (src:77-77)
GIVEN `the application is delivered by a person as agent for the subscribers to the memorandum of association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application states the agent's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) the application states the agent's name and address as required` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is delivered by a person as agent for the subscribers to the memorandum of association`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the application is delivered by a person as agent for the subscribers" (no requirement arises, fork F-C1)
    ELSE IF `the application states the agent's name and address`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must state his name and address" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:78 | (3A) The application must contain—
-- src:79 | (a) a statement of the required information about each of the subscribers to the memorandum of association (see section 9A),
-- src:80 | (b) a statement that none of the subscribers to the memorandum of association is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)),
-- src:81 | (c) if any of them would be so disqualified but for the permission of a court to act, a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying—
-- src:82 | (i) the subscriber’s name,
-- src:83 | (ii) the court by which permission was given, and
-- src:84 | (iii) the date on which permission was given, and
-- src:85 | (d) if any of them would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (designated persons under sanctions legislation) but for the authority of a licence of the kind mentioned in that section or Article, a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying—
-- src:86 | (i) the subscriber’s name, and
-- src:87 | (ii) the date on which it was issued and by whom it was issued.
@ref s 9(3A) Registration documents: what the application must contain about the subscribers (src:78-87)
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of the required information about each of the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement that none of the subscribers is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a subscriber would be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the subscriber's name, the court by which permission was given and the date on which permission was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a subscriber would be disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 but for the authority of a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the subscriber's name, the date on which the licence was issued and by whom it was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3A) the application contains the statements it must` MEANS
    IF       `the application contains a statement of the required information about each of the subscribers`
         AND `the application contains a statement that none of the subscribers is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`
         AND (   (NOT `a subscriber would be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act`)
              OR `the application contains a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the subscriber's name, the court by which permission was given and the date on which permission was given`)
         AND (   (NOT `a subscriber would be disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 but for the authority of a licence`)
              OR `the application contains a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the subscriber's name, the date on which the licence was issued and by whom it was issued`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must contain— (a) ... (d)" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1; paragraphs (c) and (d) bind only where their "if" holds, fork F-C1)

-- src:88 | (4) The application must contain—
-- src:89 | (a) in the case of a company that is to have a share capital, a statement of capital and initial shareholdings (see section 10);
-- src:90 | (b) in the case of a company that is to be limited by guarantee, a statement of guarantee (see section 11);
-- src:91 | (c) a statement of the company's proposed officers (see section 12);
-- src:92 | (d) a statement of initial significant control (see section 12A).
@ref s 9(4) Registration documents: statements of capital, guarantee, officers and significant control (src:88-92)
GIVEN `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of capital and initial shareholdings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is to be limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of initial significant control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) the application contains the statements it must` MEANS
    IF       ((NOT `the company is to have a share capital`) OR `the application contains a statement of capital and initial shareholdings`)
         AND ((NOT `the company is to be limited by guarantee`) OR `the application contains a statement of guarantee`)
         AND `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed officers`
         AND `the application contains a statement of initial significant control`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must contain— (a) ... (d)" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1; paragraphs (a) and (b) bind only in the case they name)

-- src:93 | (5) The application must also contain—
-- src:94 | (a) a statement of the intended address of the company's registered office , which must be an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2); ...
-- src:95 | (aa) a statement of the intended registered email address of the company, which must be an appropriate email address within the meaning given by section 88A(2);
-- src:96 | (b) a copy of any proposed articles of association (to the extent that these are not supplied by the default application of model articles: see section 20); and
-- src:97 | (c) a statement of the type of company it is to be and its intended principal business activities.
@ref s 9(5) Registration documents: registered office, email address, articles, type and activities (src:93-97)
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of the intended address of the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86(2) the intended address is an appropriate address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of the intended registered email address of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 88A(2) the intended email address is an appropriate email address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company proposes articles of association that are not supplied by the default application of model articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a copy of the proposed articles of association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement of the type of company it is to be and its intended principal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) the application contains what it must also contain` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the application contains a statement of the intended address of the company's registered office`
            AND `the application contains a statement of the intended registered email address of the company`
            AND ((NOT `the company proposes articles of association that are not supplied by the default application of model articles`) OR `the application contains a copy of the proposed articles of association`)
            AND `the application contains a statement of the type of company it is to be and its intended principal business activities`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must also contain— (a) ... (c)" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 86(2) the intended address is an appropriate address`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement of the intended address of the company's registered office, which must be an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2)"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER `s 88A(2) the intended email address is an appropriate email address`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an appropriate email address within the meaning given by section 88A(2)"
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement of the intended registered email address of the company, which must be an appropriate email address within the meaning given by section 88A(2)"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 88A(2) the intended email address is an appropriate email address`
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement of the intended registered email address of the company, which must be an appropriate email address within the meaning given by section 88A(2)"
             OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2)"

-- src:98 | (5A) The information as to the company's type must be given by reference to the classification scheme prescribed for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 9(5A) Registration documents: classification scheme for the company's type (src:98-98)
GIVEN `the information as to the company's type is given by reference to the classification scheme prescribed for the purposes of section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5A) the type information is given by reference to the prescribed scheme` MEANS
    IF `the information as to the company's type is given by reference to the classification scheme prescribed for the purposes of section 9`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information as to the company's type must be given by reference to the classification scheme prescribed for the purposes of this section" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:99 | (5B) The information as to the company's intended principal business activities may be given by reference to one or more categories of any prescribed system of classifying business activities.
@ref s 9(5B) Registration documents: classification of business activities (src:99-99)
GIVEN `the information is given by reference to one or more categories of a prescribed system of classifying business activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5B) the principal business activities may be given by reference to prescribed categories` MEANS
    IF `the information is given by reference to one or more categories of a prescribed system of classifying business activities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be given by reference to one or more categories of any prescribed system"

-- src:100 | (6) The application must be delivered—
-- src:101 | (a) to the registrar of companies for England and Wales, if the registered office of the company is to be situated in England and Wales (or in Wales);
-- src:102 | (b) to the registrar of companies for Scotland, if the registered office of the company is to be situated in Scotland;
-- src:103 | (c) to the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland, if the registered office of the company is to be situated in Northern Ireland.
@ref s 9(6) Registration documents: which registrar receives the application (src:100-103)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 9(6) the registrar to whom the application must be delivered` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN "the registrar of companies for England and Wales"
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN "the registrar of companies for Scotland"
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN "the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland"

@ref s 9(6) Registration documents: which registrar receives the application (src:100-103)
GIVEN `the registered office is to be situated in` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the application is delivered to the registrar of companies for` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6) the application is delivered to the right registrar` MEANS
    IF `the registered office is to be situated in` EQUALS `the application is delivered to the registrar of companies for`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be delivered— (a) to the registrar of companies for England and Wales, if the registered office of the company is to be situated in England and Wales (or in Wales); (b) ... Scotland ...; (c) ... Northern Ireland"

-- src:104 | (7) In subsection (3A)(c) “permission of a court to act” means permission of a court under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2).
@ref s 9(7) Registration documents: permission of a court to act (src:104-104)
GIVEN `s 159A(2) the permission is under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(7) the permission is permission of a court to act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 159A(2) the permission is under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the table in section 159A(2) is in another part
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“permission of a court to act” means permission of a court under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2)" (the borrowed answer is no, supplied as an input)

-- ---- s 9A: Required information about the subscribers ----------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 9A item of required information` IS ONE OF
    `s 9A the individual's name`
    `s 9A the corporate or firm name`
    `s 9A a service address`

-- src:105 | 9A Required information about the subscribers
-- src:106 | (1) The required information about a subscriber who is an individual is—
-- src:107 | (a) name;
-- src:108 | (b) a service address.
-- src:109 | (2) The required information about a subscriber that is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, is—
-- src:110 | (a) corporate or firm name;
-- src:111 | (b) a service address.
@ref s 9A(1) and (2) Required information about the subscribers: an individual, a body corporate, a firm that is a legal person (src:105-111)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
      `the subscriber is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 9A item of required information`)
`s 9A(1) the required information about a subscriber` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST (LIST `s 9A the individual's name`, `s 9A a service address`)
    WHEN `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST (LIST `s 9A the corporate or firm name`, `s 9A a service address`)
    WHEN `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST (LIST `s 9A the corporate or firm name`, `s 9A a service address`)
    WHEN `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST (LIST `s 9A the corporate or firm name`, `s 9A a service address`)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the subscriber is a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
        THEN JUST (LIST `s 9A the corporate or firm name`, `s 9A a service address`)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) names "a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed", and the text is silent on a firm that is not a legal person

-- src:112 | (3) In subsection (1) “name” means the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 9A(3) Required information about the subscribers: the individual's name (src:112-112)
GIVEN forename IS A STRING
      surname IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 9A(3) the name of an individual` MEANS
    CONCAT forename, " ", surname

-- src:113 | (4) Where a subscriber is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, that title may be stated in the application for the registration of the company instead of the subscriber’s forename and surname.
@ref s 9A(4) Required information about the subscribers: a peer or an individual known by a title (src:113-113)
GIVEN `the subscriber is a peer or an individual usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name stated in the application` IS A STRING
      forename IS A STRING
      surname IS A STRING
      title IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9A(4) the name stated for the subscriber is acceptable` MEANS
    IF `the name stated in the application` EQUALS (`s 9A(3) the name of an individual` forename surname)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the subscriber is a peer or an individual usually known by a title` AND `the name stated in the application` EQUALS title
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“name” means the individual’s forename and surname" (a title may stand instead only for a peer or an individual usually known by a title)

-- s 9A(5) (regulations that may amend this section) and s 9A(6) (affirmative resolution procedure for them) are
-- machinery: inert under reason 2 (regulation-making powers). See NOTES.md, Coverage.

-- ---- s 10: Statement of capital and initial shareholdings ------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 10(2)(c) statement for a class of shares` HAS
    `states the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the total number of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:118 | 10 Statement of capital and initial shareholdings
-- src:119 | (1) The statement of capital and initial shareholdings required to be delivered in the case of a company that is to have a share capital must comply with this section.
-- src:120 | (2) It must state—
-- src:121 | (a) the total number of shares of the company to be taken on formation by the subscribers to the memorandum of association,
-- src:122 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:123 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) to be unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:124 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:125 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:126 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:127 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
-- src:128 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 10(2) Statement of capital and initial shareholdings: what it must state (src:118-128)
GIVEN `the statement states the total number of shares of the company to be taken on formation by the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the aggregate amount (if any) to be unpaid on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements for each class of shares` IS A LIST OF `s 10(2)(c) statement for a class of shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) the statement of capital states what it must` MEANS
    IF       `the statement states the total number of shares of the company to be taken on formation by the subscribers`
         AND `the statement states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
         AND `the statement states the aggregate amount (if any) to be unpaid on those shares`
         AND all (GIVEN c YIELD     c's `states the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
                                AND c's `states the total number of shares of that class`
                                AND c's `states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class`)
                 `the statements for each class of shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must state— (a) ... (ba) ... (c) for each class of shares— (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ..." (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1; paragraph (d) is blank in this text)

-- src:129 | (3) It must contain such information as may be prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association.
@ref s 10(3) Statement of capital and initial shareholdings: identifying the subscribers (src:129-129)
GIVEN `the statement contains the information prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the statement contains the prescribed identifying information` MEANS
    IF `the statement contains the information prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must contain such information as may be prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

DECLARE `s 10(4)(a) statement for a class of shares taken by a subscriber` HAS
    `states the number of shares to be taken by the subscriber on formation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the nominal value of each share` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:130 | (4) It must state, with respect to each subscriber to the memorandum—
-- src:131 | (a) the number, nominal value (of each share) and class of shares to be taken by him on formation, and
-- src:132 | (b) the amount to be paid up and the amount (if any) to be unpaid on each share (whether on account of the nominal value of the share or by way of premium).
@ref s 10(4) Statement of capital and initial shareholdings: what it must state for each subscriber (src:130-132)
GIVEN `the statements of the shares of each class the subscriber is to take` IS A LIST OF `s 10(4)(a) statement for a class of shares taken by a subscriber`
      `the statement states the amount to be paid up and the amount (if any) to be unpaid on each share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) the statement states what it must for the subscriber` MEANS
    IF       (NOT (null `the statements of the shares of each class the subscriber is to take`))
         AND all (GIVEN s YIELD     s's `states the number of shares to be taken by the subscriber on formation`
                                AND s's `states the nominal value of each share`
                                AND s's `states the class of shares`)
                 `the statements of the shares of each class the subscriber is to take`
         AND `the statement states the amount to be paid up and the amount (if any) to be unpaid on each share`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must state, with respect to each subscriber to the memorandum— (a) ... (b) ..." (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:133 | (5) Where a subscriber to the memorandum is to take shares of more than one class, the information required under subsection (4)(a) is required for each class.
@ref s 10(5) Statement of capital and initial shareholdings: shares of more than one class (src:133-133)
GIVEN `the number of classes of shares the subscriber is to take` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of classes for which the information required under subsection (4)(a) is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the information is given for each class` MEANS
    IF `the number of classes of shares the subscriber is to take` AT MOST 1
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a subscriber to the memorandum is to take shares of more than one class" (no requirement arises, fork F-C1)
    ELSE IF `the number of classes for which the information required under subsection (4)(a) is given` AT LEAST `the number of classes of shares the subscriber is to take`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the information required under subsection (4)(a) is required for each class" (a bare "is required" not done, fork F-C1)

-- s 10(1) is the lead-in to subsections (2) to (5) ("must comply with this section"): it is covered by those functions.

-- ---- s 11: Statement of guarantee ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:134 | 11 Statement of guarantee
-- src:135 | (1) The statement of guarantee required to be delivered in the case of a company that is to be limited by guarantee must comply with this section.
-- src:136 | (2) It must contain such information as may be prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association.
@ref s 11(2) Statement of guarantee: identifying the subscribers (src:134-136)
GIVEN `the statement contains the information prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) the statement contains the prescribed identifying information` MEANS
    IF `the statement contains the information prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must contain such information as may be prescribed for the purpose of identifying the subscribers to the memorandum of association" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:137 | (3) It must state that each member undertakes that, if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member, he will contribute to the assets of the company such amount as may be required for—
-- src:138 | (a) payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member,
-- src:139 | (b) payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up, and
-- src:140 | (c) adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves,
-- src:141 | not exceeding a specified amount.
@ref s 11(3) Statement of guarantee: what it must state (src:137-141)
GIVEN `the statement states that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company if it is wound up while he is a member or within one year after he ceases to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states that the contribution is for payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states that the contribution is for payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states that the contribution is for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states a specified amount not to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(3) the statement of guarantee states what it must` MEANS
    IF       `the statement states that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company if it is wound up while he is a member or within one year after he ceases to be a member`
         AND `the statement states that the contribution is for payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member`
         AND `the statement states that the contribution is for payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up`
         AND `the statement states that the contribution is for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves`
         AND `the statement states a specified amount not to be exceeded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must state that each member undertakes that, if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member, he will contribute to the assets of the company such amount as may be required for— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..., not exceeding a specified amount" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

@ref s 11(3) Statement of guarantee: when the undertaking bites (src:137-141)
GIVEN `the date the person ceased to be a member (if the person has ceased)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the winding up of the company began` IS A DATE
      `the company is wound up while the person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(3) the undertaking applies to the member` MEANS
    IF `the company is wound up while the person is a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date the person ceased to be a member (if the person has ceased)`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person has not ceased to be a member and the company was not wound up while he is one, so the undertaking's two occasions are not met
         WHEN JUST ceased THEN
             IF       `the date the winding up of the company began` AT LEAST ceased
                  AND `the date the winding up of the company began` AT MOST (`add years` ceased 1)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

@ref s 11(3) Statement of guarantee: the most the member can be required to contribute (src:137-141)
GIVEN `the undertaking applies to the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `costs, charges and expenses of winding up, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `amount required for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the specified amount in the statement of guarantee, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(3) the most the member can be required to contribute, in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking applies to the member`
    THEN JUST (min `the specified amount in the statement of guarantee, in pounds`
                   (  `debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member, in pounds`
                    PLUS `costs, charges and expenses of winding up, in pounds`
                    PLUS `amount required for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves, in pounds`))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the undertaking is stated for a winding up "while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member"

