    IF       `the statement contains the required information about the person or persons to be the first director or directors`
         AND (    (NOT (`the company is to be a public company` OR `a person is to be the first secretary (or persons are to be joint secretaries)`))
              OR  `the statement contains the required information about the first secretary (or joint secretaries)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain the required information about— (a) ... first director or directors ...; (b) in the case of a company that is to be a private company, any person who is (or any persons who are) to be the first secretary ...; (c) in the case of a company that is to be a public company, the person who is (or the persons who are) to be the first secretary" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

