GIVEN `s 790C there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity on incorporation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement states whether, on incorporation, there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes the required particulars of any such person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(1) the statement of initial significant control states what it must` MEANS
    IF NOT `the statement states whether, on incorporation, there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must— (a) state whether, on incorporation, there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 790C there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity on incorporation`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "registrable person" and "registrable relevant legal entity" are defined in s 790C
         WHEN JUST someone THEN
             IF (NOT someone) OR `the statement includes the required particulars of any such person`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must— ... (b) include the required particulars of any such person" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:168 | (1A) If there is anyone who will be a registrable person, or a registrable relevant legal entity, in relation to the company on incorporation, the statement must also include—
-- src:169 | (a) a statement that none of them is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)),
-- src:170 | (b) if any of them would be so disqualified but for the permission of a court to act, a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying—
-- src:171 | (i) the person’s name,
-- src:172 | (ii) the court by which permission was given,
-- src:173 | (iii) the date on which permission was given, and
-- src:174 | (c) if any of them would be so disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (designated persons under sanctions legislation) but for the authority of a licence of the kind mentioned in that section or Article, a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying—
-- src:175 | (i) the person’s name, and
-- src:176 | (ii) the date on which the licence was issued and by whom it was issued.
@ref s 12A(1A) Statement of initial significant control: further statements where there is a registrable person (src:168-176)
GIVEN `s 790C there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity on incorporation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a statement that none of them is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them would be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the person's name, the court by which permission was given and the date on which permission was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them would be disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 but for the authority of a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the person's name, the date on which the licence was issued and by whom it was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(1A) the statement includes what it must where there will be a registrable person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 790C there will be anyone who is either a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity on incorporation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "registrable person" and "registrable relevant legal entity" are defined in s 790C
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If there is anyone who will be a registrable person, or a registrable relevant legal entity, in relation to the company on incorporation" (no requirement arises, fork F-C1)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `the statement includes a statement that none of them is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`
             AND (   (NOT `one of them would be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act`)
                  OR `the statement includes a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the person's name, the court by which permission was given and the date on which permission was given`)
             AND (   (NOT `one of them would be disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 but for the authority of a licence`)
                  OR `the statement includes a statement to that effect, in respect of each of them, specifying the person's name, the date on which the licence was issued and by whom it was issued`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the statement must also include— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

