-- src:204 | (2) The certificate must state—
-- src:205 | (a) the name and registered number of the company,
-- src:206 | (b) the date of its incorporation,
-- src:207 | (c) whether it is a limited or unlimited company, and if it is limited whether it is limited by shares or limited by guarantee,
-- src:208 | (d) whether it is a private or a public company, and
-- src:209 | (e) whether the company's registered office is situated in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland.
@ref s 15(2) Issue of certificate of incorporation: what the certificate states (src:204-209)
GIVEN `the certificate states the name and registered number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states the date of the company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states whether the company is a limited or unlimited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states, if the company is limited, whether it is limited by shares or limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states whether the company is a private or a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states whether the company's registered office is situated in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the certificate states what it must` MEANS
    IF       `the certificate states the name and registered number of the company`
         AND `the certificate states the date of the company's incorporation`
         AND `the certificate states whether the company is a limited or unlimited company`
         AND `the certificate states whether the company is a private or a public company`
         AND `the certificate states whether the company's registered office is situated in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland`
         AND (   (NOT (`s 3(1) the company is a limited company` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE))
              OR `the certificate states, if the company is limited, whether it is limited by shares or limited by guarantee`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must state— (a) ... (e)" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

@ref s 15(2)(c) Issue of certificate of incorporation: limited or unlimited, and by shares or by guarantee (src:207-207)
GIVEN c IS A `Company profile`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15(2)(c) what the certificate must state about the liability of the members`
`s 15(2)(c) what the certificate must state about the liability of the members` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `liability of the members`
    WHEN `liability not limited` THEN JUST `s 15(2)(c) that the company is an unlimited company`
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` THEN JUST `s 15(2)(c) that the company is a limited company limited by shares`
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` THEN JUST `s 15(2)(c) that the company is a limited company limited by guarantee`
    WHEN `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the certificate states "whether it is a limited or unlimited company, and if it is limited whether it is limited by shares or limited by guarantee", and s 3(1) says a limited company "may be limited by shares or limited by guarantee": a third kind is not provided for

@ref s 15(2)(d) Issue of certificate of incorporation: private or public company (src:208-208)
GIVEN `the application states that the company is to be a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 15(2)(d) what the certificate must state about the company's status`
`s 15(2)(d) what the certificate must state about the company's status` MEANS
    IF `the application states that the company is to be a public company`
    THEN `s 15(2)(d) that the company is a public company`
    ELSE `s 15(2)(d) that the company is a private company`

@ref s 15(2)(e) Issue of certificate of incorporation: where the registered office is situated (src:209-209)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 15(2)(e) what the certificate must state about the registered office` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN "England and Wales (or in Wales)"
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN "Scotland"
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN "Northern Ireland"

