`s 16(5) the number of shares the subscriber holds on registration` MEANS
    IF `the effects of registration have begun` AND `the company has a share capital`
    THEN JUST `the number of shares specified for the subscriber in the statement of capital and initial shareholdings`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company having a share capital, the subscribers to the memorandum become holders of the shares specified in the statement of capital and initial shareholdings"

-- src:218 | (6) The persons named in the statement of proposed officers—
-- src:219 | (a) as director, or
-- src:220 | (b) as secretary or joint secretary of the company,
-- src:221 | are deemed to have been appointed to that office unless ineligible for appointment to that office by virtue of any enactment.
@ref s 16(6) Effect of registration: the persons named in the statement of proposed officers (src:218-221)
GIVEN `the effects of registration have begun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as director, or as secretary or joint secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is ineligible for appointment to that office by virtue of any enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(6) the person is deemed to have been appointed to the office` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the effects of registration have begun` AND `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as director, or as secretary or joint secretary of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The persons named in the statement of proposed officers— (a) as director, or (b) as secretary or joint secretary of the company, are deemed to have been appointed" (as from the date of incorporation)
    ELSE IF `the person is ineligible for appointment to that office by virtue of any enactment`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are deemed to have been appointed to that office unless ineligible for appointment to that office by virtue of any enactment"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
